      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Secret Management**\n\nOkay, I'm zeroing in on defining the secret management aspect now. I need to make a solid choice for a secrets store; thinking about how to integrate it concretely. I will focus on making it identifiable within the Python script so that this file can be understood by external systems. I need to start thinking about the specific steps for authentication.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Cloud Secret Manager**\n\nI've decided Google Cloud Secret Manager is the best fit. My plan crystallizes: the `rotate_secret_version.py` file will have a function taking a secret ID and version/stage. Leveraging the Google Cloud Secret Manager client, I will integrate the `google.cloud.secretmanager_v1` library for concrete provider identification. The function will directly use the provided client to access secrets.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818726624,
          "start": 1789818725265
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
